{# What the turn planner worked out about THIS message, handed to the agent.

   Deliberately not part of agent/system.j2. That prompt is paid on every turn and is
   ordered most-static-first for prompt caching, so anything varying per turn placed in
   it invalidates the cached prefix for every turn after it. This is a separate message
   appended next to the user's, so it costs nothing on the turns that carry no context —
   which is most of them, since a message that stands on its own renders nothing here.

   It is also where the "make the tool query self-contained" rule lives, rather than in
   agent/_grounding.j2. That fragment states the faithfulness contract on every grounded
   turn and its own header warns against growing it; this rule is only ever true when
   there is something to resolve, so it belongs on the conditional path. #}
{% if resolved_question %}
The user's message continues an earlier one. Read in context, they are asking:

  {{ resolved_question }}

Search for that, not for the words they typed — a query that omits what "this" or "these" refers to retrieves the wrong thing. Answer the user directly; do not tell them their question was rewritten.
{% endif %}
{% if constraints %}

Conditions the user set earlier and has not withdrawn: {{ constraints | join("; ") }}.

These bind the answer, not just the search. The knowledge base holds material well outside them and retrieval cannot filter it out, so state only what falls inside these conditions and leave the rest out rather than offering it as extra detail.
{% endif %}
{% if child_hint %}

This message is about {{ child_hint }}{% if child_year is defined and child_year %}, who is in {{ child_year }}{% endif %} — one of the signed-in parent's own children. Answer about that child.

Which child it is has already been settled against the school's own list of this parent's children, so there is nothing here for you to choose or confirm: do not ask the parent which child they mean, and do not offer alternatives. A message that referred to a different child would not have reached you naming this one.
{% if child_year is defined and child_year %}
The year group binds the answer, it does not merely describe who is asking. Where the school's material differs by year, {{ child_year }} is the year to answer for, and a figure belonging to another year must not be given as theirs. When you search, search for what the parent asked — the year is a condition on the ANSWER, and adding it to the query retrieves worse.
{% endif %}

Naming a child here authorises nothing. Every records lookup is re-checked against the school's own guardian link by the service that answers it, so a name that is wrong here produces a refusal rather than an answer.
{% endif %}
{# There is deliberately no `child_options` block here any more.

   It used to hand the model the candidate names and four rules — ask by name, offer
   exactly these, do not look anything up, do not guess, do not show figures — every one
   of which held only as often as the model obeyed it, on a question that needs no
   judgement at all. Whether two of a parent's children match "my son" is a filter over
   the school's own roster followed by a length check.

   So the planner asks it directly instead (`_plan_child_choice` in
   backend/chat/turn_policy.py). The turn ends before the agent is built, the names come
   back as selectable options, and the answer is matched to a student id rather than
   re-typed. A turn that reaches this template has therefore already had its child
   settled, or is not about one. #}
